{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Anna.</b> Supplication, saying to HaShem: \"Anna, save!\" The priests [say it], and \"Grant success!\" — those who bring offerings to the house of HaShem [say it]. \"Blessed\" [follows]. Or the verb may be הושיעה and also הצליחה [as] coming [forms], and this is the formula of the priests, to say thus. And this is the joy and gladness mentioned above. Now the he at the end serves retrospectively, like לאורח הבא (Genesis 19:2 — 'the arriving wayfarer'), לאיש בליעל (Deuteronomy 15:2 — wait, no) לאיש בליעל, את יום השביעי (Exodus 20:8(?) — no) — and likewise the meaning: \"Anna, HaShem, save now; grant success now.\""], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 118, :notes {0 "The comment is textually difficult. The phrase 'וכן הטען' introduces a paraphrase of the verse, but the preceding biblical phrase examples and the attribution of speakers are cryptic and possibly corrupt; translated hyper-literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:40:08.185709940Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}